From: QING23qin <112809742+QING23qin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cgroup: allow namespace root to host nested controllers

DroidSpaces uses the container cgroup as the root of a cgroup namespace
while keeping its monitor process in that cgroup. The normal cgroup v2
no-internal-process rule otherwise rejects enabling domain controllers
below such a populated namespace root.

Treat the cgroup namespace root in the default hierarchy as mixable. The
real hierarchy root already has this property. This keeps the exception
scoped to the namespace root rather than weakening the rule for arbitrary
cgroups.

---
 kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c
--- a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup.c
@@ -1040,8 +1040,18 @@ static bool cgroup_is_mixable(struct cgroup *cgrp)
 	/*
 	 * Root isn't under domain level resource control exempting it from
 	 * the no-internal-process constraint, so it can serve as a thread
 	 * root and a parent of resource domains at the same time.
 	 */
-	return !cgroup_parent(cgrp);
+	if (!cgroup_parent(cgrp))
+		return true;
+
+	/*
+	 * DroidSpaces uses a container cgroup as the root of a cgroup
+	 * namespace and intentionally keeps its monitor in that cgroup.
+	 * Allow that namespace root to host nested resource domains.
+	 */
+	if (current->nsproxy && current->nsproxy->cgroup_ns &&
+	    cgrp == cset_cgroup_from_root(
+		current->nsproxy->cgroup_ns->root_cset, &cgrp_dfl_root))
+		return true;
+
+	return false;
 }
 
 /* can @cgrp become a thread root? should always be true for a thread root */
 static bool cgroup_can_be_thread_root(struct cgroup *cgrp)
